What is already in place
- MSI and MSI-X capability parsing and programming are implemented in kernel/driver/pci.c.
- pci_irq_alloc_vectors, pci_irq_free_vectors, pci_irq_vector, pci_irq_mode are exported in include/pci.h.
- Trap/IRQ dispatch path can handle dynamically registered vectors across full IRQ range.

Current blockers (code-verified)
- Most drivers still bind to legacy INTx irq_line directly.
- Virtio core still initializes vdev->irq from pci->irq_line; virtio_blk/virtio_net/virtio_gpu now override this with allocated vectors.
- NVMe intentionally disables MSI/MSI-X and operates polled-only.

